{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"Read each issue body and verify each fix on the bound final tree; preserve #880 advisory recall, #816/#822 checkpoint discipline, and reviewer worker backend contract.","packet_sha256":"90649a109efd19f4625f6cabda05a78ff5492ba1ec1d6a38d00c3c791327642f","reviewed_input_identity_sha256":"77bd02ce93f1f2c2866a1ed2138ba01c372ca480ad95cea10716c36db3aecbc7","verdict":"pass","target_observations":[{"target":"corca-ai/charness#877","verdict":"pass","summary":"The checkpoint handles both reported cases and retains the pinned empty-lane and before-edit distinctions.","evidence":["Issue #877 requires a resolved MERGE_HEAD to be committed as a whole WIP merge, or a distinct unresolved-merge blocker with conflicted paths; a clean tree with lane commits should use the branch tip.","task_run_checkpoint checks merge state before the no-scoped-change skip, rejects unresolved paths and conflict-marker paths, refuses resolved merges with out-of-scope dirty paths, and commits admitted resolved merges without a pathspec.","For non-merge state, no scoped changes still returns a skipped checkpoint; commit-only carrier state returns the head tip. task_run preserves distinct merge errors in the blocker detail.","The supplied #877 tests cover resolved and unresolved merges, mixed-scope refusal, marker detection, tip reuse, and terminal target_sha reporting. The supplied #822 tests pin known-before-edit classification for skipped checkpoints and retain unknown WIP for failed checkpoints."]},{"target":"corca-ai/charness#878","verdict":"pass","summary":"The Claude backend removes the rejected schema dialect marker and includes captured backend stderr in nonzero-exit failures.","evidence":["Issue #878 reports Claude CLI rejection of the top-level draft 2020-12 $schema and asks for the stderr cause to appear in the lifecycle reason.","reviewer_worker_backend._command parses the schema and removes only the top-level $schema key before compact JSON is passed to --json-schema.","execute_backend reads the first nonempty stderr line, bounds it to 500 characters, and includes it in the typed backend-failed message; without stderr it retains a plain exit-code message.","The supplied backend tests pin preservation of schema shape, stripping of $schema, surfaced stderr, and fallback behavior when stderr is absent or blank. The backend remains in its established command/execution/normalization owner; no lifecycle or result-contract change is introduced here."]},{"target":"corca-ai/charness#879","verdict":"pass","summary":"The path heuristic filters identifier/ref-like tokens while preserving file-shaped advisory recall; the alleged launch refusal is contradicted by the bound prelaunch and test code.","evidence":["Issue #879 asks to drop dotted identifiers and foreign slash tokens, retain paths rooted at real top-level directories or existing paths, and remove the scope-mismatch phrase switch.","_keep_candidate retains candidates with a repository top-level first segment, an existing path, or a file-shaped slash token. The parser has no scope-mismatch substring switch; supplied tests cover dotted identifiers, origin/main, task/abc, npm scope and fs/promises, plus new paths and line-number paths under real top-level directories.","The reported false-refusal premise does not hold in these bytes: task_run_plan records would_touch_outside_declared findings and warnings, while task_run_prelaunch renders them as explicitly non-blocking advisory text. run_prelaunch_gates only returns blockers for a central premise failure or acceptance-skeleton baseline; scope findings do not raise or block launch.","The supplied launch-hygiene test asserts the scope-omission marker executes and findings remain recorded, preserving #880 advisory recall. A file-shaped slash token without a repository foothold remains a suggestion as separately pinned by the #879 test."]}],"findings":[],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"The file-shaped slash fallback can still suggest an external-looking path such as zebra/qux.ts.","bin":"accepted-tradeoff","disposition":"Retained as advisory recall, consistent with #880 and the explicit #879 test; scope enforcement remains on the actual candidate."},{"concern":"Resolved merge handling commits the whole index during MERGE_HEAD.","bin":"controlled-boundary","disposition":"The checkpoint verifies conflict state and checks dirty paths against refreshed declared scope before whole-merge commit; empty lanes still skip and out-of-scope residue still blocks."},{"concern":"Stripping $schema may alter Claude schema handling beyond the reported rejection.","bin":"no-new-defect-evidence","disposition":"The backend preserves the remaining schema payload and the supplied test pins that behavior; no contradictory contract evidence appears in the reviewed bytes."}],"next_move":"No fix follow-up is indicated by the bound evidence; retain the three issue-resolution results as passing.","non_claims":["This review did not execute tests or commands; it assessed only the identity-bound semantic payload supplied in the packet.","The packet contains no evidence of a live Claude CLI invocation after the schema change."]}
